{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfaYbwBtjRHbE62g2eewu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe endpoint is decomposed sensibly — a dedicated check function, a checked exception, an escalation handler, and YAML wiring that places the check after validation and before build. That overall shape matches the house style. But a few structural issues keep it from being clean:\n\n1. **Normalization logic is duplicated / lives in two units.** The class javadoc states that `ValidateOwnerFields` \"has already normalized the request telephone to its ten digits,\" yet `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` carries its own private `normalize(...)` and re-normalizes `request.getTelephone()`. The normalization rule (strip non-digits) is now a domain rule encoded in at least two places. If the two definitions ever drift, uniqueness silently breaks. Extract the normalization into one shared place (a helper on the DTO/entity or a small util) and have both the validate step and this step call it — or, if the request telephone is genuinely already normalized by the prior step, drop the redundant re-normalization of the request here. As written it is both duplicated and self-contradictory with its own doc.\n\n2. **Error response body shape is inconsistent with the existing handler style.** The worked example and the existing `HandleOwnerNotFound` respond with `ResponseEntity<String>`. This handler instead invents an ad-hoc `ResponseEntity<Map<String, Object>>` with `Map.of(\"error\", ..., \"telephone\", ...)`. An inline map is a catch-all structure that doesn't match any established error-response convention in this codebase; a maintainer would not find it natural, and it establishes a second, divergent error-body format. Either reuse the existing `ResponseEntity<String>` message style, or introduce a proper error DTO if a structured body is wanted — not an untyped map.\n\n3. **Minor — governance level.** AGENTS.md prescribes `govern: [ readonly-transaction ]` for read-only steps; `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` only reads (`findAll`). It's given `govern: [ transaction ]`. Since the surrounding POST pipeline is a write this is defensible, but for consistency with the stated convention a read-only step should use the read-only governance.\n\n4. **Minor — method naming.** Sibling steps use descriptive method names (`validate`, `load`, `apply`). This step's public method is the generic `service`, which reads less naturally alongside them; a verb like `check` would fit the convention better.\n\nPoints 1 and 2 are the substantive ones."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10738,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10738},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3bcbd8f-3930-4c2c-ad7b-1acac61e2175","uuid":"3229229b-b2f5-4dd4-b505-2c41d632b0fe","timestamp":"2026-10-01T00:10:03.759Z","request_id":"req_011CfaYbvr3iZxATVaKD8VWQ"}
